= The Catalan State

As the CEDA enters the national government, Lluís Companys - Macià's successor at the Generalitat - proclaims the "Catalan State within the Federal Spanish Republic" from the balcony in Barcelona, in solidarity with the October rising. It is a gesture more than a plan: General Batet's troops shell the Generalitat palace and the Catalan government surrenders within hours.

The Statute of Autonomy is suspended, the Generalitat's leaders imprisoned, Catalan self-rule extinguished at gunpoint. The army has now put down an elected regional government by force and been thanked for it by Madrid - a rehearsal, and an education, for the officers who took part.

[? if catalan_autonomy <= 0 : Everything Catalonia won in 1932 is gone; the reckoning for that will come. ?]
